w he got them if  he got them through a whistleblower  then he didn't hack them i mean that's  just not true it just depends  but the fact that they admit that these  slack communications exist and they seem  to be  verifying that they are real is an even  worse  look for the company than anything that  they've admitted publicly so that's  where the story is now  um it's not believable that white hat jr  is only going after people  who are you know being unfair to them  they are silencing  all criticism that comes their way it's  very clear from the messages that  they're reporting anything and  everything that can be construed as  criticism at all  you can be sure that they'll report this  video they'll report any video that  talks about them  and frankly that's the part that bothers  me the most because in order to root out  corruption scams to tell the frauds  from the people who are honest you have  to have that criticism you have to have  the open exchange even when it's sort of  intense and it can be loaded with some  pretty heavy language  you have to have it you have to have it  for the people who are buying into this  stuff  this is a multi-multi-multi-million  dollar company  and it needs to be exposed to criticism  to see if it holds up  and right now they're not doing that my  hope is as always that the truth comes  out  thanks for watching and we may do a  follow-up on this as more information  comes out  see you next time and don't forget to  smash like  and subscribe thank you up
 

